---
metadata:
  title: "Mr & Mrs Charles Dickens - Her Story | Annie Elliot"
  description: "After twenty-two years of marriage, Charles Dickens banished his wife Kate from their home. This is Kate's story: a poignant self-portrait of a woman struggling to achieve peace of mind. A novel by Annie Elliot."
  canonical: "https://annieelliot.co.uk/"
  pageType: "book"
---

<section id="about" class="u-container">
  <h1>Mr & Mrs Charles Dickens</h1>
  <h2>Her Story</h2>
  <div>
    <div class="u-grid main-grid">
      <div>
        <p>
          After twenty-two years of marriage, Charles Dickens banished his wife,
          Kate from their home and nine children and wrecked her reputation to
          protect his own when he fell in love with an eighteen-year-old
          actress.
        </p>

        <p>
          This is Kate's story: a poignant self-portrait of a woman struggling
          to achieve peace of mind by making sense of a marriage that defined,
          but nearly destroyed her. Sifting through her husband's letters after
          his sudden death she relives the happy times they shared but also
          speaks up for herself to expose the darker side of the man the world
          reveres.
        </p>

        <p>
          On her deathbed, Kate asked her daughter to give Charles's letters to
          the British Museum 'so the world may know he loved me once.' This
          novel fulfils her dying wish and restores her to history as more than
          a famous author's discarded wife. It bestows on Kate the respect,
          dignity, agency and voice she was denied in life.
        </p>

        <reviews></reviews>

        <nav class="related-links" aria-label="Related links">
          <p>Learn more about <a href="/author/">the author, Annie Elliot</a>, or <a href="/events/">find upcoming book events</a>.</p>
        </nav>
      </div>

      <div class="cover">
        <img
          webc:is="eleventy-image"
          src="assets/images/cover.jpg"
          alt="Mr & Mrs Charles Dickens book cover"
        />
        <!-- <button type="button">Preorder now!</button> -->
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

